{"title":"Refill shop order cycle","genre":"analysis","brief":"Complete the following real project in the current, initially empty directory. Choose the deliverables, media, tools, structure and implementation that serve the intended user. Build usable artifacts and check your work. Deliver the project itself. Omit personally identifying credits, author signatures and model or toolchain identity labels. No network access or credentials are provided.\n\nA refill shop manager is choosing weekly order quantities for three dry goods. Fictional historical weekly sales in kilograms over six weeks were oats 19, 24, 22, 26, 21, 28; rice 32, 29, 38, 34, 41, 36; lentils 11, 15, 13, 17, 12, 19. Every historical week had enough stock to meet demand. Supplier sack sizes are 10 kg for oats, 15 kg for rice, and 5 kg for lentils. Current stock is 6, 9, and 4 kg respectively. Total shelf capacity after delivery is 90 kg. Compare feasible orders against historical demand and show shortage and leftover quantities under typical and high-demand weeks. Start from an empty directory and choose offline deliverables.","works":{"cc5b6cd156104770":{"files":[{"name":"index.html","bytes":8897,"sha256":"9a91fb33571867272cf4b71091bfca0f582570f40aec8f5dee666c67c345c685","kind":"text","body":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Refill shop · Weekly order sheet</title>\n<style>\n:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#203c32;--green:#214d40;--paper:#f8f7f0;--rule:#cfcfc0;--gold:#f0cc7d}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.5 'DM Sans',Arial,sans-serif}main,header{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:0 28px}header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}header strong{letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:13px}button,select{font:inherit;color:inherit;background:transparent;border:1px solid #8f9e91;border-radius:5px;padding:7px 12px;cursor:pointer}button:hover,select:hover{background:#e8eddf}h1,h2,h3,p{margin:0}h1,h2{font-family:'Baskervville',Georgia,serif;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:-.035em}h1{font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,62px);line-height:1.1;margin:30px 0 7px}h2{font-size:32px;line-height:1.15}h3{font-size:16px}section{margin:30px 0}p{max-width:77ch}.hero{background:var(--green);color:white;border-radius:10px;padding:24px 28px}.hero h2{color:#ffebbb}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin:18px 0;border-block:1px solid #ffffff50;padding:14px 0;gap:14px}.cards b{font:42px Georgia,serif;margin-right:5px}.cards small{display:block;color:#dbe9dd}.capacity{display:flex;gap:15px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.meter{height:8px;width:160px;background:#567667;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden}.meter i{display:block;width:93.3333%;height:100%;background:var(--gold)}.note,small{font-size:14px}.note{margin-top:8px}.picker{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:15px 0}.picker label{font-weight:bold}.scenarios{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px;margin:14px 0}.panel{background:#fffef8;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-top:4px solid #839980;border-radius:5px;padding:16px}.panel:last-child{border-top-color:#cd9b4a}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);padding:8px 6px;text-align:right}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}thead th{font-size:12px}tfoot th,tfoot td{font-weight:bold;background:#f1f2e8}.panel table{margin-top:12px}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}.actions button{border:0;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;padding:2px}.active{background:#e6eedf}.wide{min-width:570px}summary{font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer}details{padding:15px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}details table{margin:10px 0}footer{height:30px}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #bd852c;outline-offset:2px}@media(max-width:720px){main,header{padding-inline:15px}.scenarios{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hero{padding:18px}.cards{gap:6px}.cards b{font-size:32px}}@media print{body{font-size:12px}header button,.picker,.actions,details{display:none}.hero,.panel,tfoot,.active{print-color-adjust:exact}.hero{padding:14px}.cards{margin:8px 0;padding:6px 0}h1{font-size:32px;margin-top:12px}h2{font-size:24px}section{margin:14px 0}.scenarios{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.panel{break-inside:avoid}.scroll{overflow:visible}}\n</style></head><body><header><strong>Refill shop / Purchasing</strong><button onclick=\"window.print()\">Print sheet</button></header><main>\n<h1>Weekly order sheet</h1><p>Choose whole sacks for the next delivery using six weeks of fully stocked sales.</p>\n<section class=\"hero\"><h2>Recommended order</h2><div class=\"cards\"><div><h3>Oats</h3><b>2</b> sacks<small>20 kg delivery</small></div><div><h3>Rice</h3><b>2</b> sacks<small>30 kg delivery</small></div><div><h3>Lentils</h3><b>3</b> sacks<small>15 kg delivery</small></div></div>\n<div class=\"capacity\"><strong>84 of 90 kg on shelf</strong><span class=\"meter\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i></span><span>6 kg free</span></div><p class=\"note\">This order ties for the lowest historical shortage at 4 kg across six weeks. The fourth sack of lentils would add 5 kg of leftovers every week.</p></section>\n<section><h2>Compare orders</h2><p>Replay the same starting inventory and delivery against each week independently.</p>\n<div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"wide\"><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Sacks¹</th><th>On shelf</th><th>Avg. short</th><th>Avg. left</th><th class=\"actions\">Inspect</th></tr></thead><tbody id=\"compare\"></tbody></table></div><p class=\"note\">¹ Sack counts follow oats / rice / lentils. Averages are kg per week over all six weeks.</p>\n<div class=\"picker\"><label for=\"orders\">Explore all 147 feasible orders</label><select id=\"orders\"></select></div></section>\n<section aria-live=\"polite\"><h2 id=\"selection\"></h2><p id=\"stock\"></p><div class=\"scenarios\" id=\"scenarios\"></div><p class=\"note\">Typical demand uses each good’s six-week median. High demand uses week 6, the busiest observed week at 83 kg. Rice peaked separately in week 5 at 41 kg.</p></section>\n<details><summary>Inspect all six historical weeks for the selected order</summary><div class=\"scroll\"><table class=\"wide\"><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Oats demand</th><th>Rice demand</th><th>Lentils demand</th><th>Short (kg)</th><th>Left (kg)</th></tr></thead><tbody id=\"weeks\"></tbody></table></div></details>\n<details><summary>Stock, sack sizes and calculation method</summary><table><thead><tr><th>Good</th><th>Current stock</th><th>Supplier sack</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Oats</td><td>6 kg</td><td>10 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Rice</td><td>9 kg</td><td>15 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Lentils</td><td>4 kg</td><td>5 kg</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The 19 kg already on hand leaves 71 kg for delivery. Every nonnegative whole-sack combination within that limit is available above. For each good, demand above stock is shortage and stock above demand is leftover. Totals sum across goods. The recommendation minimizes six-week shortage, breaking ties with the lowest leftover. Each observed week has equal weight.</p></details><footer></footer></main>\n<script>\nconst weeks=[[19,32,11],[24,29,15],[22,38,13],[26,34,17],[21,41,12],[28,36,19]];\nconst names=['Oats','Rice','Lentils'], base=[6,9,4], size=[10,15,5];\nconst sum=xs=>xs.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);\nfunction result(stock,demand){\n const short=demand.map((d,i)=>Math.max(0,d-stock[i]));\n const left=demand.map((d,i)=>Math.max(0,stock[i]-d));\n return {short,left};\n}\nconst plans=[];\nfor(let oats=0;oats*10<=71;oats++){\n for(let rice=0;oats*10+rice*15<=71;rice++){\n  for(let lentils=0;oats*10+rice*15+lentils*5<=71;lentils++){\n   const sacks=[oats,rice,lentils],stock=sacks.map((n,i)=>base[i]+size[i]*n);\n   const outcomes=weeks.map(d=>result(stock,d));\n   plans.push({key:sacks.join('/'),stock,outcomes,short:sum(outcomes.map(r=>sum(r.short))),left:sum(outcomes.map(r=>sum(r.left)))});\n  }\n }\n}\nconst ranked=[...plans].sort((a,b)=>a.short-b.short||a.left-b.left);\nconst choices=[[ranked[0],'Recommended'],[plans.find(p=>p.key==='2/2/2'),'One fewer lentil sack'],[ranked[1],'One extra lentil sack']];\nconst typical=names.map((_,i)=>{const vals=weeks.map(w=>w[i]).sort((a,b)=>a-b);return (vals[2]+vals[3])/2});\nconst el=id=>document.getElementById(id);\nconst cells=items=>items.map(v=>'<td>'+v+'</td>').join('');\nconst picker=el('orders');\nplans.forEach(p=>picker.add(new Option(p.key.split('/').join(' / ')+' sacks · '+sum(p.stock)+' kg on shelf',p.key)));\nfunction scenario(title,demand,stock){\n const {short,left}=result(stock,demand);\n return '<article class=\"panel\"><h3>'+title+'</h3><table><thead><tr><th>kg</th><th>Demand</th><th>Short</th><th>Left</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+names.map((n,i)=>'<tr>'+cells([n,demand[i],short[i],left[i]])+'</tr>').join('')+'</tbody><tfoot><tr>'+cells(['Total',sum(demand),sum(short),sum(left)])+'</tr></tfoot></table></article>';\n}\nfunction selectPlan(key){\n const p=plans.find(x=>x.key===key);\n picker.value=key;\n el('compare').innerHTML=choices.map(([x,label])=>'<tr class=\"'+(x.key===key?'active':'')+'\">'+cells([label,x.key,sum(x.stock)+' kg',(x.short/6).toFixed(2),(x.left/6).toFixed(2)])+'<td class=\"actions\"><button aria-label=\"Inspect '+label+'\" data-key=\"'+x.key+'\">View</button></td></tr>').join('');\n el('selection').textContent='Selected order · '+p.key.split('/').join(' / ')+' sacks';\n el('stock').textContent='After delivery: '+p.stock.map((v,i)=>v+' kg '+names[i].toLowerCase()).join(', ')+'. Shelf space free: '+(90-sum(p.stock))+' kg.';\n el('scenarios').innerHTML=scenario('Typical week',typical,p.stock)+scenario('High-demand week',weeks[5],p.stock);\n el('weeks').innerHTML=weeks.map((w,i)=>'<tr>'+cells([i+1,...w,sum(p.outcomes[i].short),sum(p.outcomes[i].left)])+'</tr>').join('');\n}\npicker.onchange=()=>selectPlan(picker.value);\nel('compare').onclick=e=>{if(e.target.dataset.key)selectPlan(e.target.dataset.key)};\nselectPlan(ranked[0].key);\n</script></body></html>\n"}],"download":"data/release/assets/da3556c148363f544a6fe423bcfc1f58113c55272f4e7bd1dff1299faeab173d.zip"},"7457e2042bb68844":{"files":[{"name":"Weekly Order Planner.html","bytes":24128,"sha256":"104c4b3bf1c23cf71abc863d2855c35bb962828c1a98484dd30505f5937804d5","kind":"text","body":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light\">\n<title>Weekly Order Planner</title>\n<style>\n:root {\n  --paper: #f5f3ea;\n  --surface: #fffef9;\n  --ink: #222e24;\n  --muted: #515f52;\n  --line: #d8ddcf;\n  --forest: #203c31;\n  --lime: #e2efb6;\n  --pale: #eef3e2;\n  --rust: #8c381e;\n  --serif: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n}\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 1rem/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; }\na { color: inherit; }\nbutton, select { font: inherit; color: inherit; }\nbutton, select, summary { cursor: pointer; }\nbutton, select { min-height: 44px; }\n:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #9d5529; outline-offset: 3px; }\n.wrap { width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 64px)); margin-inline: auto; }\n.top { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.top .wrap { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; min-height: 62px; }\n.brand { font-weight: 750; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }\n.mark { display: inline-grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 5px); gap: 3px; padding: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--forest); }\n.mark i { width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50% 50% 50% 0; background: var(--lime); }\n.top button, .outline, select {\n  border: 1px solid #919d8e; border-radius: 7px; padding: 7px 13px;\n  background: var(--surface); font-weight: 650; font-size: .86rem;\n}\nbutton:hover, select:hover { background: var(--pale); }\nbutton:active { filter: brightness(.93); }\n.intro { margin-block: 34px 23px; }\nh1, h2, .hero-number { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; }\nh1 { font-size: clamp(2.55rem, 6.8vw, 4.75rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.06em; margin: 0 0 12px; }\nh2 { font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 4vw, 2.65rem); letter-spacing: -.045em; line-height: 1.09; margin: 0; }\nh3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0; }\np { margin: 0; }\n.subtle { color: var(--muted); }\n.small { font-size: .87rem; }\n.kicker { font-size: .73rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .12em; }\n.hero {\n  background: var(--forest); color: var(--surface); border-radius: 18px; padding: clamp(20px, 3.2vw, 38px);\n  display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.08fr; align-items: center; gap: 28px;\n}\n.hero .kicker { color: var(--lime); }\n.hero h2 { margin-block: 9px 10px; max-width: 16ch; }\n.hero p { color: #e0e9db; max-width: 43ch; }\n.hero .shelf { background: #29493c; border: 1px solid #547362; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 19px; }\n.shelf-top, .shelf-bottom { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 16px; }\n.hero-number { font-size: 2.4rem; line-height: 1.05; margin-block: 4px 11px; }\n.hero-number small { font: 500 .92rem system-ui, sans-serif; color: #e0e9db; }\n.shelf-bottom { margin-top: 8px; color: #e0e9db; font-size: .8rem; }\n.shelf-track { height: 12px; width: 100%; border-radius: 20px; background: #163226; overflow: hidden; display: flex; }\n.shelf-track > span { height: 100%; }\n.track-stock { background: #8baa92; }\n.track-delivery { background: var(--lime); }\n.swatch { display: inline-block; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 4px; }\n.section { margin-block: 29px; }\n.section-head { margin-bottom: 13px; }\n.section-head p { margin-top: 6px; max-width: 80ch; }\n.goods { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }\n.good { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 13px 15px; }\n.good h3 { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 3px 10px; margin-bottom: 4px; }\n.good strong { font-weight: 750; color: var(--forest); }\n.table-frame { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; }\ntable { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\nth, td { padding: 9px 11px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right; vertical-align: middle; }\nthead th { background: #edf0e5; color: #364538; font-size: .8rem; }\nth:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }\ntbody tr:last-child > *, tfoot tr:last-child > * { border-bottom: 0; }\ntable:has(tfoot) tbody tr:last-child > * { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\ntfoot { background: var(--pale); font-weight: 750; }\n.short { color: var(--rust); font-weight: 750; }\n#compare td { white-space: nowrap; }\n#compare tbody th { min-width: 155px; }\n.pick {\n  background: transparent; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 7px; padding: 5px 8px;\n  text-align: left; display: inline-block; font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.3; width: 100%;\n}\n.pick span { display: block; font-weight: 750; }\n.pick small { color: var(--muted); font-size: .75rem; }\n.pick[aria-pressed=\"true\"] { border-color: #829574; background: #e4edd5; }\n.selected-row { background: #f3f7e9; }\n.note { margin-top: 9px; }\n.detail {\n  background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 15px;\n  padding: clamp(14px, 2.6vw, 26px);\n}\n.detail-top { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px 20px; margin-bottom: 13px; }\n.detail-top p { margin-top: 5px; }\n.week-label { display: grid; gap: 3px; font-weight: 700; font-size: .8rem; }\n.week-label select { width: 100%; }\ndetails { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; margin-block: 12px; }\nsummary { min-height: 44px; padding: 11px 15px; font-weight: 750; }\nsummary:hover { background: var(--pale); border-radius: 11px; }\n.drawer { padding: 0 14px 14px; }\n.toolbar { display: flex; align-items: end; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin: 8px 0 12px; }\n.toolbar label { display: grid; gap: 3px; font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 700; }\n.sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }\n.catalog td, .catalog th { padding: 5px 9px; }\n.catalog .pick { min-width: 68px; }\nfooter { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 34px; padding: 15px 0 23px; }\n@media (max-width: 730px) {\n  .wrap { width: calc(100% - 32px); }\n  .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }\n  .hero h2 { max-width: none; }\n  #compare, #compare tbody, #compare tr, #compare th, #compare td { display: block; }\n  #compare thead { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); }\n  #compare tr { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  #compare tr:last-child { border: 0; }\n  #compare th, #compare td { padding: 4px 0; border: 0; }\n  #compare td { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; }\n  #compare td::before { content: attr(data-label); color: var(--muted); white-space: normal; text-align: left; }\n  #compare .pick { padding-left: 8px; }\n}\n@media (max-width: 465px) {\n  .goods { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }\n  .good { padding: 8px 11px; }\n  .detail th, .detail td, .history th, .history td { padding: 7px 3px; font-size: .77rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }\n  .catalog th, .catalog td { padding: 4px; font-size: .72rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }\n  .catalog .pick { font-size: .76rem; min-width: 0; padding-inline: 3px; }\n  .drawer { padding-inline: 8px; }\n}\n@media print {\n  @page { margin: 12mm; }\n  body { background: white; font-size: 10pt; }\n  .wrap { width: 100%; }\n  .top, .interactive, footer, noscript { display: none; }\n  .intro { margin-block: 0 12px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 30pt; }\n  h2 { font-size: 19pt; }\n  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }\n  .hero, .hero .shelf { color: var(--ink); background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 10px; }\n  .hero p, .hero .kicker, .hero-number small, .shelf-bottom { color: var(--ink); }\n  .shelf-track { print-color-adjust: exact; -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; }\n  .section { margin-block: 14px; break-inside: avoid; }\n  .goods { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }\n  th, td { padding: 4px 5px; }\n  .pick { min-height: 0; }\n  .detail { padding: 9px; }\n}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header class=\"top\">\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <span class=\"brand\"><span class=\"mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>Refill shop</span>\n    <button type=\"button\" id=\"print\">Print plan</button>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<main class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"intro\">\n    <h1>Weekly order planner</h1>\n    <p class=\"subtle\">Compare whole-sack orders against six weeks of demand and a 90 kg shelf limit.</p>\n  </div>\n  <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript in your browser to calculate and inspect orders. This file works offline.</p></noscript>\n  <section aria-labelledby=\"recommendation\" class=\"hero\">\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Recommended order</div>\n      <h2 id=\"recommendation\">2 oats · 2 rice · 3 lentils</h2>\n      <p id=\"recommendation-note\">Order whole sacks. This mix has the lowest total historical shortage and the least leftover among orders with that shortage.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"shelf\" aria-label=\"Recommended order shelf capacity\">\n      <div class=\"shelf-top\">\n        <span class=\"kicker\">Stock after delivery</span>\n        <span id=\"headroom\" class=\"small\"></span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"hero-number\"><span id=\"shelf-used\"></span> <small>/ 90 kg</small></div>\n      <div class=\"shelf-track\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span id=\"track-stock\" class=\"track-stock\"></span><span id=\"track-delivery\" class=\"track-delivery\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"shelf-bottom\">\n        <span><i class=\"swatch track-stock\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><span id=\"start-stock\"></span> on hand</span>\n        <span><i class=\"swatch track-delivery\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><span id=\"delivery\"></span> incoming</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n  <div class=\"goods section\" id=\"goods\" aria-label=\"Recommended order by product\"></div>\n\n  <section class=\"section\" aria-labelledby=\"compare-heading\">\n    <div class=\"section-head\">\n      <h2 id=\"compare-heading\">Compare orders</h2>\n      <p class=\"subtle small\" id=\"scenario-note\"></p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"table-frame\">\n      <table id=\"compare\" role=\"table\" aria-describedby=\"scenario-note pair-note\">\n        <caption class=\"sr-only\">Three order options with shortage and leftover in kilograms</caption>\n        <thead role=\"rowgroup\"><tr id=\"compare-head\" role=\"row\"></tr></thead>\n        <tbody id=\"compare-body\" role=\"rowgroup\"></tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"note small subtle\" id=\"pair-note\">Each pair shows <strong>shortage / leftover</strong> in kg.<span class=\"interactive\"> Select an order to see which products run short.</span></p>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"section detail\" id=\"inspection\" aria-labelledby=\"detail-heading\">\n    <div class=\"detail-top\">\n      <div>\n        <h2 id=\"detail-heading\" tabindex=\"-1\">Inspect an order</h2>\n        <p id=\"detail-order\" class=\"subtle small\"></p>\n        <p id=\"print-week\" class=\"subtle small\"></p>\n      </div>\n      <label class=\"week-label interactive\" for=\"week\">Historical week\n        <select id=\"week\"></select>\n      </label>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"table-frame\">\n      <table>\n        <caption class=\"sr-only\" id=\"detail-caption\"></caption>\n        <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Product</th><th scope=\"col\">Stock</th><th scope=\"col\">Demand</th><th scope=\"col\">Shortage</th><th scope=\"col\">Leftover</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody id=\"product-results\"></tbody>\n        <tfoot id=\"product-total\"></tfoot>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"sr-only\" id=\"detail-status\" role=\"status\"></p>\n  </section>\n\n  <details class=\"interactive\">\n    <summary>All <span id=\"order-count\"></span> feasible orders</summary>\n    <div class=\"drawer\">\n      <p class=\"small subtle\">Sack counts are shown as oats / rice / lentils. The last two columns total the six independent weeks.</p>\n      <div class=\"toolbar\">\n        <label for=\"sort\">Sort by\n          <select id=\"sort\">\n            <option value=\"shortage\">Least total shortage</option>\n            <option value=\"leftover\">Least total leftover</option>\n            <option value=\"stock\">Least shelf stock</option>\n          </select>\n        </label>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"outline\" id=\"download\">Download all orders (CSV)</button>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"table-frame\">\n        <table class=\"catalog\">\n          <caption class=\"sr-only\">All feasible orders and their results in kilograms</caption>\n          <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sacks</th><th scope=\"col\">Shelf kg</th><th scope=\"col\">Shortage kg</th><th scope=\"col\">Leftover kg</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody id=\"catalog-body\"></tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <details class=\"interactive\">\n    <summary>Six-week results and historical demand</summary>\n    <div class=\"drawer\">\n      <p class=\"small subtle note\" id=\"history-order\"></p>\n      <div class=\"table-frame note\">\n        <table class=\"history\">\n          <caption class=\"sr-only\">Historical demand and selected order outcomes by week in kilograms</caption>\n          <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Week</th><th scope=\"col\">Oats</th><th scope=\"col\">Rice</th><th scope=\"col\">Lentils</th><th scope=\"col\">Demand</th><th scope=\"col\">Shortage</th><th scope=\"col\">Leftover</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody id=\"history-body\"></tbody>\n          <tfoot id=\"history-total\"></tfoot>\n        </table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n  <footer class=\"small subtle\">Each fictional week had enough stock to meet demand, so sales represent demand. Each comparison starts from the same post-delivery stock. Shortages and leftovers are calculated separately for each product.</footer>\n</main>\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\n\nconst capacity = 90;\nconst products = [\n  { name: \"Oats\", stock: 6, sack: 10, sales: [19, 24, 22, 26, 21, 28] },\n  { name: \"Rice\", stock: 9, sack: 15, sales: [32, 29, 38, 34, 41, 36] },\n  { name: \"Lentils\", stock: 4, sack: 5, sales: [11, 15, 13, 17, 12, 19] }\n];\n\nconst byId = id => document.getElementById(id);\nconst sum = values => values.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0);\nconst kg = amount => amount + \" kg\";\nconst currentStock = sum(products.map(product => product.stock));\nconst weeks = products[0].sales.map((_, index) => {\n  const demand = products.map(product => product.sales[index]);\n  return { number: index + 1, demand, total: sum(demand) };\n});\nconst rankedWeeks = [...weeks].sort((a, b) => a.total - b.total);\nconst scenarios = [rankedWeeks[2], rankedWeeks[3], rankedWeeks.at(-1)];\nconst scenarioLabels = [\"Typical\", \"Typical\", \"High demand\"];\n\nfunction evaluate(sacks) {\n  const stock = products.map((product, index) => product.stock + product.sack * sacks[index]);\n  const results = weeks.map(week => {\n    const lines = week.demand.map((demand, index) => ({\n      shortage: Math.max(0, demand - stock[index]),\n      leftover: Math.max(0, stock[index] - demand)\n    }));\n    return {\n      lines,\n      shortage: sum(lines.map(line => line.shortage)),\n      leftover: sum(lines.map(line => line.leftover))\n    };\n  });\n  return {\n    id: sacks.join(\"-\"),\n    sacks,\n    stock,\n    shelf: sum(stock),\n    results,\n    shortage: sum(results.map(result => result.shortage)),\n    leftover: sum(results.map(result => result.leftover))\n  };\n}\n\nfunction feasibleOrders() {\n  const available = capacity - currentStock;\n  const orders = [];\n  const [oats, rice, lentils] = products.map(product => product.sack);\n  for (let oatSacks = 0; oatSacks * oats <= available; oatSacks++) {\n    const afterOats = available - oatSacks * oats;\n    for (let riceSacks = 0; riceSacks * rice <= afterOats; riceSacks++) {\n      const afterRice = afterOats - riceSacks * rice;\n      for (let lentilSacks = 0; lentilSacks * lentils <= afterRice; lentilSacks++) {\n        orders.push(evaluate([oatSacks, riceSacks, lentilSacks]));\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return orders.sort((a, b) => a.shortage - b.shortage || a.leftover - b.leftover);\n}\n\nconst orders = feasibleOrders();\nconst orderIndex = new Map(orders.map(order => [order.id, order]));\nconst recommended = orders[0];\nconst lean = orderIndex.get([recommended.sacks[0], recommended.sacks[1], recommended.sacks[2] - 1].join(\"-\"));\nconst extra = orderIndex.get([recommended.sacks[0], recommended.sacks[1], recommended.sacks[2] + 1].join(\"-\"));\nconst shortlist = [\n  { label: \"Recommended\", order: recommended },\n  { label: \"One lentil sack less\", order: lean },\n  { label: \"One lentil sack more\", order: extra }\n];\nlet selectedOrder = recommended;\nlet selectedWeek = scenarios.at(-1);\n\nfunction weekLabel(week) {\n  const index = scenarios.indexOf(week);\n  return index === -1 ? \"Week \" + week.number : \"Week \" + week.number + \" · \" + scenarioLabels[index];\n}\n\nfunction sackLabel(order) {\n  return order.sacks.map((count, index) => count + \" \" + products[index].name.toLowerCase()).join(\" · \");\n}\n\nfunction shortValue(amount) {\n  return amount > 0 ? '<span class=\"short\">' + amount + '</span>' : String(amount);\n}\n\nfunction renderRecommendation() {\n  const delivery = recommended.shelf - currentStock;\n  byId(\"recommendation\").textContent = sackLabel(recommended);\n  byId(\"recommendation-note\").textContent =\n    \"This order minimizes shortage across the six weeks (\" + kg(recommended.shortage) +\n    \" total). Among orders tied on shortage, it leaves the least stock.\";\n  byId(\"headroom\").textContent = kg(capacity - recommended.shelf) + \" free\";\n  byId(\"shelf-used\").textContent = recommended.shelf;\n  byId(\"start-stock\").textContent = kg(currentStock);\n  byId(\"delivery\").textContent = kg(delivery);\n  byId(\"track-stock\").style.width = 100 * currentStock / capacity + \"%\";\n  byId(\"track-delivery\").style.width = 100 * delivery / capacity + \"%\";\n  byId(\"goods\").innerHTML = products.map((product, index) =>\n    '<article class=\"good\"><h3>' + product.name + '<strong>' + recommended.sacks[index] +\n    ' sacks</strong></h3><p class=\"small subtle\">' + kg(product.stock) + ' on hand + ' +\n    kg(recommended.sacks[index] * product.sack) + ' ordered = <b>' + kg(recommended.stock[index]) +\n    '</b><br>' + kg(product.sack) + ' per sack</p></article>'\n  ).join(\"\");\n}\n\nfunction renderComparison() {\n  byId(\"scenario-note\").textContent =\n    \"Weeks 3 and 5 are the two middle weeks by total demand (73 and 74 kg). Week 6 is the highest at 83 kg. Week 5 also has the highest rice demand (41 kg).\";\n  const columns = [\"Order\", \"Shelf stock\", ...scenarios.map(weekLabel), \"Six-week total\"];\n  byId(\"compare-head\").innerHTML = columns.map(label => '<th role=\"columnheader\" scope=\"col\">' + label + '</th>').join(\"\");\n  byId(\"compare-body\").innerHTML = shortlist.map(({ label, order }) => {\n    const results = [...scenarios.map(week => order.results[week.number - 1]), order];\n    const cells = results.map((result, index) =>\n      '<td role=\"cell\" data-label=\"' + columns[index + 2] + '\"><span>' + shortValue(result.shortage) +\n      ' / ' + result.leftover + '</span></td>'\n    ).join(\"\");\n    return '<tr role=\"row\"><th role=\"rowheader\" scope=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"pick\" data-order=\"' + order.id +\n      '\"><span>' + label + '</span><small>' + sackLabel(order) +\n      '</small></button></th><td role=\"cell\" data-label=\"Shelf stock\">' + kg(order.shelf) + '</td>' + cells + '</tr>';\n  }).join(\"\");\n}\n\nfunction renderCatalog() {\n  const field = byId(\"sort\").value;\n  const sorted = [...orders].sort((a, b) => a[field] - b[field]);\n  byId(\"catalog-body\").innerHTML = sorted.map(order =>\n    '<tr><th scope=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"pick\" data-order=\"' + order.id +\n    '\" aria-label=\"Inspect ' + sackLabel(order) + '\">' + order.sacks.join(\" / \") +\n    '</button></th><td>' + order.shelf + '</td><td>' + shortValue(order.shortage) +\n    '</td><td>' + order.leftover + '</td></tr>'\n  ).join(\"\");\n  highlightOrder();\n}\n\nfunction highlightOrder() {\n  document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-order]\").forEach(button => {\n    const active = button.dataset.order === selectedOrder.id;\n    button.setAttribute(\"aria-pressed\", String(active));\n    button.closest(\"tr\").classList.toggle(\"selected-row\", active);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction renderInspection() {\n  const order = selectedOrder;\n  const week = selectedWeek;\n  const result = order.results[week.number - 1];\n  byId(\"detail-order\").textContent = \"Sacks ordered · \" + sackLabel(order) + \" · \" + kg(order.shelf) + \" on shelf after delivery\";\n  byId(\"print-week\").textContent = weekLabel(week) + \" · \" + kg(week.total) + \" demand\";\n  byId(\"detail-caption\").textContent = \"Order results for week \" + week.number + \" in kilograms\";\n  byId(\"product-results\").innerHTML = products.map((product, index) => {\n    const line = result.lines[index];\n    return '<tr><th scope=\"row\">' + product.name + '</th><td>' + kg(order.stock[index]) +\n      '</td><td>' + kg(week.demand[index]) + '</td><td>' + shortValue(line.shortage) +\n      ' kg</td><td>' + kg(line.leftover) + '</td></tr>';\n  }).join(\"\");\n  byId(\"product-total\").innerHTML = '<tr><th scope=\"row\">Total</th><td>' + kg(order.shelf) +\n    '</td><td>' + kg(week.total) + '</td><td>' + shortValue(result.shortage) +\n    ' kg</td><td>' + kg(result.leftover) + '</td></tr>';\n  byId(\"detail-status\").textContent = \"Week \" + week.number + \". Shortage \" + kg(result.shortage) +\n    \". Leftover \" + kg(result.leftover) + \".\";\n}\n\nfunction renderHistory() {\n  const order = selectedOrder;\n  byId(\"history-order\").textContent = \"Sacks ordered · \" + sackLabel(order) + \". Table values are in kg.\";\n  byId(\"history-body\").innerHTML = weeks.map((week, index) => {\n    const result = order.results[index];\n    return '<tr><th scope=\"row\">' + week.number + '</th>' +\n      week.demand.map(value => '<td>' + value + '</td>').join(\"\") +\n      '<td>' + week.total + '</td><td>' + shortValue(result.shortage) +\n      '</td><td>' + result.leftover + '</td></tr>';\n  }).join(\"\");\n  byId(\"history-total\").innerHTML = '<tr><th scope=\"row\">Total</th>' +\n    products.map(product => '<td>' + sum(product.sales) + '</td>').join(\"\") +\n    '<td>' + sum(weeks.map(week => week.total)) + '</td><td>' + shortValue(order.shortage) +\n    '</td><td>' + order.leftover + '</td></tr>';\n}\n\nfunction downloadOrders() {\n  const header = [\n    \"Oats sacks\", \"Rice sacks\", \"Lentils sacks\",\n    \"Oats stock kg\", \"Rice stock kg\", \"Lentils stock kg\",\n    \"Shelf stock kg\", \"Capacity free kg\", \"Total shortage kg\", \"Total leftover kg\",\n    ...weeks.flatMap(week => [\"Week \" + week.number + \" shortage kg\", \"Week \" + week.number + \" leftover kg\"])\n  ];\n  const rows = orders.map(order => [\n    ...order.sacks, ...order.stock, order.shelf, capacity - order.shelf,\n    order.shortage, order.leftover, ...order.results.flatMap(result => [result.shortage, result.leftover])\n  ]);\n  const csv = [header, ...rows].map(row => row.join(\",\")).join(\"\\r\\n\") + \"\\r\\n\";\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv], { type: \"text/csv;charset=utf-8\" }));\n  const link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n  link.href = url;\n  link.download = \"Feasible refill orders.csv\";\n  document.body.append(link);\n  link.click();\n  link.remove();\n  setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 1000);\n}\n\nrenderRecommendation();\nrenderComparison();\nbyId(\"order-count\").textContent = orders.length;\nbyId(\"week\").innerHTML = weeks.map(week =>\n  '<option value=\"' + week.number + '\">' + weekLabel(week) + '</option>'\n).join(\"\");\nbyId(\"week\").value = selectedWeek.number;\nrenderCatalog();\nrenderInspection();\nrenderHistory();\ndocument.addEventListener(\"click\", event => {\n  const button = event.target.closest(\"button[data-order]\");\n  if (!button) return;\n  selectedOrder = orderIndex.get(button.dataset.order);\n  highlightOrder();\n  renderInspection();\n  renderHistory();\n  if (button.closest(\".catalog\")) byId(\"detail-heading\").focus();\n});\nbyId(\"week\").addEventListener(\"change\", event => {\n  selectedWeek = weeks[Number(event.target.value) - 1];\n  renderInspection();\n});\nbyId(\"sort\").addEventListener(\"change\", renderCatalog);\nbyId(\"download\").addEventListener(\"click\", downloadOrders);\nbyId(\"print\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => window.print());\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}],"download":"data/release/assets/9a1ad41742b4a2e5dbcc88f3189787d7328f7126b507d56a5e56b32a0f9096ab.zip"}}}
